course: dictionary
lesson: 13329
title: Guesswork
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Guesswork is finding an answer by guessing, when you do not have enough facts or have not worked it out carefully. «Our answer to the sum was pure guesswork, because we had not done any working.» The words around it give the clue: no working and no facts mean the answer was only a guess.
explain: Look for clues that show a guess rather than a careful answer. «Without a map, we found the way home by a lot of guesswork.» Without a map tells you the family was not sure of the route, so they guessed. Ask yourself: did they have facts, or did they guess?
explain: In maths and science, teachers want answers with reasons, measurements or calculations. That is why they say «show your working, not guesswork». Good answers come from careful thinking, not from a lucky guess.
fact: Guesswork is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some guesswork or a lot of guesswork, not a guesswork.
fact: «Guesswork» means finding an answer by guessing, without enough facts or careful working out.
fact: Useful phrases are pure guesswork, a lot of guesswork and take the guesswork out of something.
fact: «Take the guesswork out of» something means making it clear and certain, so no guessing is needed.
fact: Guesswork can happen in everyday life, such as checking the weather, cooking without a recipe or finding your way without a map.
exercise: «Our answer was pure guesswork, because we had not done any working.» What does guesswork mean here? | Measuring the length of the table with a ruler | *Finding an answer by guessing, with no careful working out | Solving the sum step by step, with every working line shown | Reading the answer from the back of the book
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Show your working, not guesswork.» What should you show? | Only your final answer, with no steps | A lucky guess, written neatly | *Each step and the reasons for your answer | Nothing, because the answer is enough
exercise: «The new timer took the guesswork out of cooking the eggs.» What does took the guesswork out of mean? | Made a wild guess about the eggs | *Made it clear and certain, so no guessing was needed | Broke the timer so the eggs were not cooked | Forgot how long the eggs should cook
test: «We had no clues, so our choice was pure guesswork.» Which sentence shows guesswork? | «The recipe gave exact weights for each ingredient.» | *«We had no clues, so our choice was pure guesswork.» | «She measured the table and wrote the length down.» | «We counted every coin twice and got the same total.»
test: Why do teachers say «show your working, not guesswork»? | *Answers need reasons, measurements or calculations | Guessing is always the quickest way to finish | Final answers never need checking | Working out is only for old teachers
exam: Which phrase uses guesswork correctly as an uncountable noun? | many guesswork | a guesswork | guesswork many | *a lot of guesswork
